<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 35 0 R/T(1\) One 'step' is 0.1% and the number of steps is rounded to the nearest whole step \(this is what TODO 1 in Task 7 asks\). 2\) The assignment does not give an SNF range, so I assumed 7.0-10.0 % to reject nonsense values; it is a named constant and easy to change. 3\) Payments are rounded to 2 decimals \(paise\). 4\) Two shifts per day, so a farmer has up to 10 x 2 = 20 entries in a ten-day period. 5\) Farmer ID is text. 6\) Zero litres is valid \(farmer supplied nothing\) but negative litres is not.)/E(1\) One 'step' is 0.1% and the number of steps is rounded to the nearest whole step \(this is what TODO 1 in Task 7 asks\). 2\) The assignment does not give an SNF range, so I assumed 7.0-10.0 % to reject nonsense values; it is a named constant and easy to change. 3\) Payments are rounded to 2 decimals \(paise\). 4\) Two shifts per day, so a farmer has up to 10 x 2 = 20 entries in a ten-day period. 5\) Farmer ID is text. 6\) Zero litres is valid \(farmer supplied nothing\) but negative litres is not.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[41]>>
