356 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 38 0 R/T(Three unexpected results demonstrated: \(1\) \(4.2-3.5\)/0.1 is not exactly 7; \(2\) int\(\(3.1-3.5\)/0.1\) gives -3 instead of -4 because int\(\) truncates toward zero; \(3\) round\(2.5\) = 2 and round\(-2.5\) = -2 \(ties go to the even number\), and also -7 // 2 = -4 and -2 ** 2 = -4. Conclusion: round\(\) is the correct choice for step counts. floor\(\) is correct here only by luck \(a value like 6.999999 would give 6\); int\(\) is wrong for negative values. Time: all three are O\(1\) per call \(round 72 ns, int 58 ns, floor 38 ns in my run\) and use O\(1\) space.)/E(Three unexpected results demonstrated: \(1\) \(4.2-3.5\)/0.1 is not exactly 7; \(2\) int\(\(3.1-3.5\)/0.1\) gives -3 instead of -4 because int\(\) truncates toward zero; \(3\) round\(2.5\) = 2 and round\(-2.5\) = -2 \(ties go to the even number\), and also -7 // 2 = -4 and -2 ** 2 = -4. Conclusion: round\(\) is the correct choice for step counts. floor\(\) is correct here only by luck \(a value like 6.999999 would give 6\); int\(\) is wrong for negative values. Time: all three are O\(1\) per call \(round 72 ns, int 58 ns, floor 38 ns in my run\) and use O\(1\) space.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

357 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 38 0 R/T(Explanations)/E(Explanations)/Pg 14 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

358 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 38 0 R/T(Precedence and associativity \(high to low\): ** \(right-to-left: 2**3**2 = 2**\(3**2\) = 512\), unary minus, * / // % \(left-to-right\), + - \(left-to-right\), comparisons, not, and, or. Because ** binds tighter than unary minus, -2 ** 2 = -\(2**2\) = -4, while \(-2\) ** 2 = 4.)/E(Precedence and associativity \(high to low\): ** \(right-to-left: 2**3**2 = 2**\(3**2\) = 512\), unary minus, * / // % \(left-to-right\), + - \(left-to-right\), comparisons, not, and, or. Because ** binds tighter than unary minus, -2 ** 2 = -\(2**2\) = -4, while \(-2\) ** 2 = 4.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

359 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 38 0 R/T(\(4.2 - 3.5\) / 0.1: 4.2 and 3.5 and 0.1 are inexact in binary, so the result on my machine is 7.000000000000002 \(the assignment mentions a similar 7.000000000000001-type result\) instead of 7. Using round\(\) gives the nearest whole step count \(7\), so the tiny error does not matter.)/E(\(4.2 - 3.5\) / 0.1: 4.2 and 3.5 and 0.1 are inexact in binary, so the result on my machine is 7.000000000000002 \(the assignment mentions a similar 7.000000000000001-type result\) instead of 7. Using round\(\) gives the nearest whole step count \(7\), so the tiny error does not matter.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[26]>>
endobj

360 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 38 0 R/T(round\(\) vs int\(\) vs math.floor\(\) for negative values: round\(\) goes to the nearest integer \(ties to even: round\(2.5\)=2, round\(-2.5\)=-2\); int\(\) cuts off the decimals, i.e. goes toward zero \(int\(-2.7\) = -2\); math.floor\(\) always goes down \(floor\(-2.7\) = -3\). They agree for positive non-tie values like 2.7 only partly \(round 3, int 2, floor 2\).)/E(round\(\) vs int\(\) vs math.floor\(\) for negative values: round\(\) goes to the nearest integer \(ties to even: round\(2.5\)=2, round\(-2.5\)=-2\); int\(\) cuts off the decimals, i.e. goes toward zero \(int\(-2.7\) = -2\); math.floor\(\) always goes down \(floor\(-2.7\) = -3\). They agree for positive non-tie values like 2.7 only partly \(round 3, int 2, floor 2\).)/Pg 14 0 R/K[27]>>
endobj

361 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 38 0 R/T(Comparison chaining: 2.0 <= fat <= 7.0 means \(2.0 <= fat\) and \(fat <= 7.0\) but fat is evaluated once. The output shows it is True for 2.0, 4.0 and 7.0 and False for 1.9 and 7.1. Boolean operators: and \(both true\), or \(at least one true\), not \(reverses\). Example of a rejection test: \(fat < 2.0\) or \(fat > 7.0\).)/E(Comparison chaining: 2.0 <= fat <= 7.0 means \(2.0 <= fat\) and \(fat <= 7.0\) but fat is evaluated once. The output shows it is True for 2.0, 4.0 and 7.0 and False for 1.9 and 7.1. Boolean operators: and \(both true\), or \(at least one true\), not \(reverses\). Example of a rejection test: \(fat < 2.0\) or \(fat > 7.0\).)/Pg 14 0 R/K[28]>>
endobj

