415 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 39 0 R/T(1. input\(\) returns a string because the keyboard only produces characters; Python cannot know whether '8' is a number, a name or an ID, so it always returns text and the programmer converts explicitly with int\(\) or float\(\). 2. int\('8'\) = 8, float\('8.5'\) = 8.5; int\('8.5'\) raises ValueError \(shown above\). 3. Invalid inputs: '8,5' \(comma instead of decimal point\) and 'eight' both fail float\(\) with ValueError and are rejected. 4. Validation: either check the text before converting \(strip, then check that it contains only digits and at most one '.'\), or convert and catch the error; after conversion also check the range \(litres >= 0, fat 2.0-7.0\).)/E(1. input\(\) returns a string because the keyboard only produces characters; Python cannot know whether '8' is a number, a name or an ID, so it always returns text and the programmer converts explicitly with int\(\) or float\(\). 2. int\('8'\) = 8, float\('8.5'\) = 8.5; int\('8.5'\) raises ValueError \(shown above\). 3. Invalid inputs: '8,5' \(comma instead of decimal point\) and 'eight' both fail float\(\) with ValueError and are rejected. 4. Validation: either check the text before converting \(strip, then check that it contains only digits and at most one '.'\), or convert and catch the error; after conversion also check the range \(litres >= 0, fat 2.0-7.0\).)/Pg 15 0 R/K[41]>>
endobj

