492 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 40 0 R/T(Time complexity per entry: both approaches read the string once, so O\(L\) where L is the length of the text; as the text is short \(a few characters\) this is effectively O\(1\) per entry and O\(n\) for n entries. Measured: for a valid number try/except is fastest \(84 ns\) because no exception occurs; for invalid text raising and catching an exception is slower \(401-617 ns\) than the string check \(about 150-270 ns\). The try/except approach is shorter and accepts everything float\(\) accepts \(the 'Easier to Ask Forgiveness than Permission' style\); the string check is stricter but you must write the rules yourself and may reject valid forms such as '1e2'.)/E(Time complexity per entry: both approaches read the string once, so O\(L\) where L is the length of the text; as the text is short \(a few characters\) this is effectively O\(1\) per entry and O\(n\) for n entries. Measured: for a valid number try/except is fastest \(84 ns\) because no exception occurs; for invalid text raising and catching an exception is slower \(401-617 ns\) than the string check \(about 150-270 ns\). The try/except approach is shorter and accepts everything float\(\) accepts \(the 'Easier to Ask Forgiveness than Permission' style\); the string check is stricter but you must write the rules yourself and may reject valid forms such as '1e2'.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

