1138 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 49 0 R/T(1. What changed: \(i\) the analyser gives fat and SNF with two decimal places \(e.g. 3.77%\), so readings are finer than the 0.1% step; \(ii\) from April to June the base rate is Rs 32.00 and each fat step is worth Rs 0.45 \(SNF step unchanged at 0.30\); \(iii\) a farmer supplying more than 500 litres in ten days receives a bonus of Rs 0.50 per litre.)/E(1. What changed: \(i\) the analyser gives fat and SNF with two decimal places \(e.g. 3.77%\), so readings are finer than the 0.1% step; \(ii\) from April to June the base rate is Rs 32.00 and each fat step is worth Rs 0.45 \(SNF step unchanged at 0.30\); \(iii\) a farmer supplying more than 500 litres in ten days receives a bonus of Rs 0.50 per litre.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

1139 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 49 0 R/T(2. What must be modified: Constants: one rate card is no longer enough - two cards \(normal and April-June\) plus BONUS_THRESHOLD_LITRES = 500 and BONUS_PER_LITRE = 0.50. Expressions: step counts can no longer be rounded to a whole step \(3.77% is 2.7 steps\). Functions: rate_per_litre and payout need the rate card as a parameter; a new select_rate_card\(month\) and bonus\(total_litres\) are needed; ten_day_total must add the bonus; validation must accept 2-decimal readings.)/E(2. What must be modified: Constants: one rate card is no longer enough - two cards \(normal and April-June\) plus BONUS_THRESHOLD_LITRES = 500 and BONUS_PER_LITRE = 0.50. Expressions: step counts can no longer be rounded to a whole step \(3.77% is 2.7 steps\). Functions: rate_per_litre and payout need the rate card as a parameter; a new select_rate_card\(month\) and bonus\(total_litres\) are needed; ten_day_total must add the bonus; validation must accept 2-decimal readings.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

1140 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 49 0 R/T(3. Effect of two-decimal readings on steps and rounding: step counts become fractional \(0.27 / 0.1 = 2.7\). If the old nearest-whole-step rule is kept, nearby readings get the same price and prices are off by up to half a step \(Rs 0.20/litre for fat\), and exact ties \(x.5 steps\) arise. Float arithmetic also makes these fractional steps inexact, so Decimal is needed. Rates such as 33.605 need an explicit rounding rule \(half up, to paise\).)/E(3. Effect of two-decimal readings on steps and rounding: step counts become fractional \(0.27 / 0.1 = 2.7\). If the old nearest-whole-step rule is kept, nearby readings get the same price and prices are off by up to half a step \(Rs 0.20/litre for fat\), and exact ties \(x.5 steps\) arise. Float arithmetic also makes these fractional steps inexact, so Decimal is needed. Rates such as 33.605 need an explicit rounding rule \(half up, to paise\).)/Pg 25 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

