1704 0 obj
<</Title(Expected = the exact decimal total; actual = the float total. They differ in the 10th-14th significant digits because each float addition rounds to the nearest binary value, and these tiny errors accumulate over more additions \(differences of about 1e-10 for 300, 1e-8 for 6,000, and 5e-7 for 150,000 payments\). Decimal is exact but about 1.1-1.9 times slower; even for 150,000 payments it takes only about 31 ms, so the speed cost is not a problem.)/Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1684 0 R>>
endobj

