<</Title(2. Safe rate revision: change the values in the single rate-card place only \(never inside formulas or functions\); record the effective date and keep the old card for re-processing old periods; rerun the automated tests \(Task 9/12\) before using the new rates; do not change rates in the middle of a payment cycle.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1617 0 R/Prev 1686 0 R/Next 1729 0 R>>
endobj

1708 0 obj
<</Title(4. Can it support 150,000 farmers? Yes for computation. Measured: 150,000 entries are priced in about 0.39 s \(2.6 microseconds per entry, growing linearly: 300 -> 0.8 ms, 6,000 -> 14.6 ms\). One ten-day cycle for 150,000 farmers is about 150,000 x 20 = 3,000,000 entries, estimated by linear extrapolation at about 8 seconds, which is acceptable for a batch job. The weak point is memory if all 3,000,000 entries are loaded as Decimal tuples at once \(rough estimate: more than 1 GB\), so the data should be read and processed in a stream \(file/database row by row, running total per farmer\), as in Task 8.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1617 0 R/Prev 1729 0 R/Next 1687 0 R>>
endobj

