<</Title(test_calculator.py\); assert condition, message stops the program with an AssertionError naming the failing case. One command reruns all tests in milliseconds, so after every change \(for example a rate revision\) the whole suite can be rerun with almost no effort. The cost is the one-time effort of writing the tests; the time to rerun is O\(number of tests\) of machine time instead of human time.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1748 0 R/Prev 1771 0 R>>
