<</Title(1. Import forms: import milkrate loads the module and you use names as milkrate.payout\(...\), so there is no clash with your own names. from milkrate import payout copies only the name payout into your namespace so you call payout\(...\) directly \(shorter, but could shadow another payout\). import milkrate as mr imports the whole module under a short alias, mr.payout\(...\).)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1863 0 R/Next 1897 0 R>>
endobj

1883 0 obj
<</Title(4. Standard modules: math gives functions such as floor\(\), isfinite\(\); decimal gives the exact Decimal type and rounding modes. They are installed with Python, imported with 'import math' / 'from decimal import Decimal'. 5. Module search: Python looks for a module in sys.modules \(already imported\), then in the folder of the running script \(sys.path[0]\), then the other folders listed in sys.path \(PYTHONPATH, standard library, site-packages\) - the first match wins. So milkrate.py must be in the same folder as the script \(or in a folder on sys.path\), and you should not name your file like a standard module \(e.g. math.py\) because it would be found first.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1863 0 R/Prev 1898 0 R>>
endobj

